  "findings": [
    "Saved outputs, states and layer statistics replay exactly; loss and all gradients are finite. The error name alone does not establish numeric overflow.",
    "Sixty candidate logits above 80 in the failure batch are all background. At epoch1 threshold 4, the batch has 4 TP, 519 FP and 56 FN.",
    "The epoch2 first-warning snapshot at batch820 also has five background events above 80; this is not the earlier epoch1 true-positive warning pattern.",
    "Frozen epoch1 weights already produce a head burst of 325 on train_098 windows0..5; frozen failure weights produce326 on the same prefix. This is not sufficient evidence of a new global epoch2 runaway.",
    "The observed epoch1 online-training maximum228 was not a bound for its final frozen weights on all training inputs. Previous health-check coverage missed this hard prefix.",
    "Current spike regularization measures only support-averaged stem and hidden rates. Its gradient with respect to head.weight is unused; the failure-batch weighted spike term is only about3.4e-7.",
    "The largest positive logit combines foreground pre-voltage37.74 with negative background pre-voltage-73.96 before bias; only constraining positive spike counts would not directly constrain both signed readout tails.",
    "Partial-snapshot Dev IoU improves but high-density IoU worsens at its selected operating point. Neither global collapse nor ANN-level accuracy is established."
  ],
